WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:09.040
In the nation's capital, a full-dress premiere for the Soviet film, The Cranes are Flying,

00:09.040 --> 00:14.040
Carole Baker is one of the Hollywood luminaries present, with Eric Johnston representing the

00:14.040 --> 00:19.680
U.S. film industry, which will distribute this and six more Russian films here.

00:19.680 --> 00:24.840
Also turning out in force are Washington officialdom and State Department figures, William S. B.

00:24.840 --> 00:34.440
Lacy, special assistant for East-West cultural exchanges, and U.S. I.A. chief George V. Allen.

00:34.440 --> 00:38.960
This premiere, matched by the gala opening in Moscow of a major American film, marks

00:38.960 --> 00:44.560
the opening of the first Soviet-American cultural exchange program in a widely popular medium,

00:44.560 --> 00:49.940
Motion Pictures. It does not of itself mark a major thaw in the Cold War, but the presence

00:49.940 --> 00:54.600
of Secretary of State Herter signifies the importance and hope attached to the exchange,

00:54.600 --> 00:56.480
which will reach millions in each country.

